From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: eval-retry of several logs from one eval runs their
 tasks concurrently under max_tasks

`eval_retry()` called `eval_async()` once per log and awaited each in turn,
so retrying the logs of an eval that ran several tasks at once (for example
two task-arg variants under `max_tasks=2`) ran them one after another. The
display says "Running 1 tasks" once per log, and a resumed run loses the
batching its tasks shared on the model server.

`eval_async()` refuses concurrent calls, so the retry now puts logs into one
call: logs with the same `run_id` and equal eval settings (model spec as the
log records it, generate config, limits, max_tasks, ...) run as the tasks of
one eval, each `PreviousTask` carrying its own task args. Logs of separate
evals, or with different settings, still run as evals of their own, one after
another, and results come back in the order the logs were given.

Tests: `test_eval_retry_runs_several_logs_concurrently_under_max_tasks` fails
without the change (the retried tasks do not overlap in time);
`test_eval_retry_runs_logs_with_different_models_one_after_another` checks
that a multi-model eval's logs keep their own models.

