 Note also that `eval_retry()` does not overwrite the previous log file, but rather creates a new one (preserving the `task_id` from the original file).
 
+You can retry several logs at once. Logs written by the same eval with the same settings (model, generation config, limits and so on) are retried together as one eval, so `max_tasks` runs their tasks concurrently as it did in the original eval. Logs from separate evals, or with different settings, are retried one eval after another.
+
